# Byte-exact text is compiled into the binary with `include_str!` and compared
# against LF snapshots at test time. On a Windows checkout these must not turn
# into CRLF: a single converted newline changes the prompt's size (1014 -> 1034
# bytes) and breaks the byte-exact snapshot, the size budgets and the generated
# reference blocks on every OS. Force LF in the worktree on all platforms for
# the three embedded text families (docs, snapshots, source files). Other
# file types (Windows scripts in particular) keep Git's default handling.
*.md text eol=lf
*.snapshot text eol=lf
*.rs text eol=lf
